data: {"type":"response.completed","sequence_number":1403,"safety_buffering":false,"response":{"input_transformations":[],"id":"resp_0b5b7f39f0ea9b2e016b029446466487d1976037b817f79e6a","object":"response","created_at":1795331142,"completed_at":1795331203,"status":"completed","background":false,"frequency_penalty":0.0,"presence_penalty":0.0,"moderation":null,"model":"gpt-6.1-sol","access_programs":{"cyber":"standard"},"previous_response_id":null,"instructions":"Review the entire batch of functional capability requests against actual conditions. Compare function, prerequisites, inputs, costs and effects, not names. Reuse equivalent implemented capabilities. A reasonable missing capability must enter development with a concrete specification covering state, executable behavior, costs, ongoing effects, geometry/collision/interaction, presentation/event binding, public schema, learning, dependencies and migration. Missing current operations or resources is not a reason for permanent rejection. No activity category or era name is automatically forbidden. For complex requests, identify actual prerequisites and an executable precursor. Do not prescribe an applicant's future activities, give rescue stock or count proposed products as existing.\nWellbeing is bounded and personal, not achievement accumulation. New mental sources require successful events, applicability, amount/cap, duration or maintenance conditions, repetition/cooldown, and a consistent rationale from experience. Requesting, learning, labels and narrative never award happiness. Repeated enjoyment may be legitimate; do not require novelty. Never reward duplicate functional sources under aliases. Health/survival remain independent. Physical comfort uses real hunger, health, fatigue and temperature; proposed shade/insulation must have real effects. Social/reproductive requests require actual participant consent/actions, persistent identities/relations, ongoing care and costs; one actor cannot act for others, and